<h1>Data protection statement</h1>
<div class="rte">
<p>Tourism Association &#34;Hiking Hotels in Europe&#34; Thank you for your interest in our hotel association and the information about the protection of your personal data.</p>
<p>The protection of your personal data is very important to us. We therefore process your data exclusively on the basis of the legal provisions (GDPR 2018, TKG 2021). In this privacy policy, we inform you about the most important aspects of data processing on our website.</p>
<p>If the website offers the option of entering personal or business data (such as email addresses, names, addresses, and similar), the disclosure of this data by the user is expressly voluntary. The user thus agrees that, in this case, their data will be recorded electronically and – unless revoked in writing – used for the own mailings of the tourism association &#34;Wanderhotels in Europa,&#34; e.V. and its partners. Despite careful content control, we assume no liability for the content of external links. The operators of the linked pages are solely responsible for their content.</p>
<h3>Contact</h3>
<p>The following is responsible for processing personal data on this website:</p>
<p><strong>Tourism Association &#34;Wanderhotels in Europa&#34;, e.V. (hiking hotels in Europe)</strong><br>Headquarters: 9900 Lienz, Südtiroler Platz 2/3rd floor<br>ZVR number: 611052592</p>
<p>E <a title="Email – Wanderhotels" href="&#109;&#97;&#105;&#108;&#116;&#111;&#58;&#105;&#x6E;&#102;&#x6F;&#64;&#x77;&#97;&#x6E;&#100;&#x65;&#114;&#x68;&#111;&#x74;&#101;&#x6C;&#115;&#x2E;&#99;&#x6F;&#109;" target="_blank" rel="noopener">&#105;&#x6E;&#102;&#x6F;&#64;&#x77;&#97;&#x6E;&#100;&#x65;&#114;&#x68;&#111;&#x74;&#101;&#x6C;&#115;&#x2E;&#99;&#x6F;&#109;</a><br>T <a title="Call – Wanderhotels" href="tel:+43485264611" target="_blank" rel="noopener">+43 (0)4852 64611</a></p>
<p><strong>VAT number: ATU 40197407</strong></p>
<h3>Principles</h3>
<p>The tourism association &#34;Wanderhotels in Europa,&#34; e.V. takes all necessary measures to ensure the protection of your data and to maintain confidentiality, and uses your data in compliance with legal regulations, in particular the GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) and the TKG (Telecommunications Act). This means that your data will only be used if there is legal permission or your consent.</p>
<p>We take organizational, contractual, and technical security measures in accordance with the state of the art to ensure that the legal framework is complied with and to protect your data against accidental or intentional manipulation, loss, destruction, or access by unauthorized persons.</p>
<p>We would like to point out that data transmission over the Internet (e.g. when communicating by email) can have security gaps. Complete protection against access by third parties is therefore not possible. If you use this website without otherwise transmitting data to us (e.g. by registering or using a contact form), we collect technically necessary data that is automatically transmitted to our server, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>IP address – This is transmitted in encrypted form.</li>
<li>Date and time of the request.</li>
<li>Content of the request.</li>
<li>Access status/HTTP status code.</li>
<li>Browser type.</li>
<li>Language and version of the browser software</li>
<li>Operating system</li>
</ul>
<p>This is technically necessary in order to display our website to you. We also use the data to ensure the security and stability of our website. The legal basis for the collection is Art. 6 (1) lit. f GDPR.</p>
<h3>Processing of personal data</h3>
<h4>Personal data</h4>
<p>Personal data is data that can be used to identify or make identifiable the person concerned (e.g., name, address, telephone number, email address, IP address, etc.).</p>
<p>We only process personal data that you provide to us on the basis of your inquiry, booking, order of advertising material, or participation in competitions, or for the use of our other services, and which is necessary for us to provide our services to you.</p>
<h4>Pure contact request</h4>
<p>If you contact us via the form on our website or by email, we will store the data you provide for the purpose of processing your request and in case of any subsequent questions. We will not pass on this data without your consent.</p>
<h4>Use and disclosure of personal data in the event of a request, order, or booking</h4>
<p>We use the personal data you provide when making inquiries, ordering advertising materials of any kind, making bookings, or participating in competitions exclusively for the purpose of processing your inquiry, order, or booking. The data you provide is necessary for the implementation of pre-contractual measures or for the fulfillment of the contract. Without this data, we cannot conclude the contract with you.</p>
<p>As a matter of principle, only persons involved in the inquiry, order, booking, or competition process will have access to your personal data. All employees entrusted with data processing are obliged to maintain the confidentiality of your data. We will not sell the personal data you provide to third parties or market it in any other way. Your personal data will only be passed on to third parties or otherwise transferred if this is necessary for business processing (inquiry or booking to the hotel) or if you have given your prior consent. We will not use the data you provide to us in inquiries, orders, bookings, or when participating in competitions, nor other personal data received from you in this context, to send you targeted advertising, unless you have expressly agreed to this in the form of written or digital consent.</p>
<h4>Order processing</h4>
<p>Based on agreements we have concluded specifically for this purpose regarding the processing of personal data, your data will be processed on our behalf by</p>
<ul>
<li>INCERT eTourismus GmbH &amp; Co KG, based in Linz</li>
<li>Kubeos GmbH, Gewerbestraße 15, A-5151 Nussdorf</li>
</ul>
<p>within the scope of order processing in accordance with Art. 28 GDPR and the relevant legal requirements in the context of support measures. Within the scope of their service provision, the aforementioned order processors have access to your data, but may only use it for the purpose of these support measures for us and not for their own purposes.</p>
<h4>Transfer of data</h4>
<p>We may share the data collected with other external processors who process data on our behalf in accordance with the law. Only data necessary for processing is passed on, and this is deleted by the processor after processing is complete:</p>
<ul>
