</ul>
<p>This data is not passed on to external companies and is only evaluated internally; it may be passed on to the competent authorities for criminal prosecution.</p>
<h3>Cookies</h3>
<p>Our website uses cookies. These are small text files that are stored on your device with the help of your browser. They do not cause any damage.</p>
<p>We use cookies to make our website user-friendly, and they are necessary to enable some functions. Some cookies remain stored on your device until you delete them. They enable us to recognize your browser the next time you visit.</p>
<p>If you do not want this, you can set your browser to inform you about the setting of cookies and only allow this in individual cases.</p>
<p>If you deactivate cookies, the functionality of our website may be limited.</p>
<h3>Web analysis</h3>
<p>Our website uses functions of the web analysis service Google Analytics provided by Google Inc. (1600 Amphitheatre Parkway Mountain View, CA 94043, USA). Cookies are used for this purpose, which enable an analysis of the use of the website by its users. The information generated in this way is transferred to the provider&#39;s server and stored there. You can prevent this by setting your browser so that no cookies are stored, or by refusing your consent in the cookie notice. In addition, a general opt-out is possible via browser plugin: https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout?hl&#61;de</p>
<p>Your IP address is recorded, but immediately pseudonymized (e.g., by deleting the last 8 bits). This means that only a rough localization is possible.</p>
<p>Data processing is carried out on the basis of the legal provisions of § 96 (3) TKG and Art. 6 (1) lit. a (consent) and/or f (legitimate interest) of the GDPR.</p>
<p>Our concern in terms of the GDPR (legitimate interest) is to improve our offering and our website. Since the privacy of our users is important to us, user data is pseudonymized.</p>
<p>Further details on Google&#39;s terms of use and data protection can be found at http://www.google.com/analytics/terms/de.html and https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245?hl&#61;de.</p>
<h3>Newsletter</h3>
<p>You have the option of subscribing to our newsletter via our website. To do so, we need your email address and your declaration that you agree to receive the newsletter. Once you have registered for the newsletter, we will send you a confirmation email with a link to confirm your registration. The newsletter is processed by Sendinblue GmbH, Köpenicker Straße 126, 10179 Berlin; For this purpose, we will pass on your email address and, if provided, your name. Sendinblue is also subject to the European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and will process your data with due care. Further details can be found at: <a href="https://de.sendinblue.com/legal/privacypolicy/">https://de.sendinblue.com/legal/privacypolicy/ </a></p>
<p>You can unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time, either via the unsubscribe link included in the footer of each newsletter or by sending an informal email to our contact address above. We will then immediately delete your data in connection with the newsletter dispatch.</p>
<h3>reCAPTCHA Cloudfare</h3>
<p>To protect against spam and abuse, we use the <strong>Cloudflare reCAPTCHA</strong> service (hereinafter &#34;reCAPTCHA&#34;) from <strong>Cloudflare, Inc. </strong>, 101 Townsend Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA, on our website when you register for our newsletter.</p>
<p>reCAPTCHA is used to ensure that the newsletter registration is carried out by a natural person and not by an automated program.</p>
<p>The legal basis for the processing of this data is <strong>Art. 6 (1) lit. f GDPR</strong> (legitimate interest).. Our legitimate interest lies in ensuring the security of our website and preventing misuse by automated programs.</p>
<p>Further information on Cloudflare&#39;s privacy policy can be found here:<br><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/de-de/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
<h3>Mapbox</h3>
<p>We use the Mapbox map service to provide map data. This involves the use of cookies that contain user settings and data. You can prevent this by disabling cookies in your browser.</p>
<p>Further details on Mapbox&#39;s terms of use and privacy policy can be found at <a href="https://www.mapbox.com/legal/tos/">https://www.mapbox.com/legal/tos/</a> and <a href="https://www.mapbox.com/legal/privacy/">https://www.mapbox.com/legal/privacy/</a></p>
<h3>Mouse tracking</h3>
<p>Our concern in terms of the GDPR (legitimate interest) is to improve our offering and our website. We therefore use Hotjar to better understand the needs of our users and to optimize the offering on this website. Hotjar&#39;s technology helps us to better understand our users&#39; experiences (e.g., how much time users spend on which pages, which links they click on, what they like and dislike, etc.), which helps us to tailor our offerings to our users&#39; feedback. Hotjar uses cookies (see above) and other technologies to collect information about our users&#39; behavior and their devices (in particular, the device&#39;s IP address (only collected and stored in anonymized form), screen size, device type (unique device identifiers), information about the browser used, location (country only), preferred language for displaying our website). Hotjar stores this information in a pseudonymized user profile. The information is not used by Hotjar or us to identify individual users or merged with other data about individual users. For more information, please see Hotjar&#39;s privacy policy: <a href="https://www.hotjar.com/legal/policies/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">https://www.hotjar.com/legal/policies/privacy</a>.</p>
<h3>YouTube</h3>
<p>To provide videos, we use the video service YouTube LLC 901 Cherry Ave., 94066 San Bruno, CA, USA, a company of Google Inc., Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA.</p>
<p>Each time a page is accessed, a connection to YouTube is established to download video information and the video player; since we operate YouTube in &#34;extended data protection mode,&#34; cookies are only set when the video is actually played. You can prevent this by disabling cookies in your browser.</p>
<p>Further details can be found at https://www.google.de/intl/de/policies/privacy/</p>
<h3>Facebook and Instagram</h3>
<p>Our website uses functions of the social network Facebook provided by Facebook Ireland Ltd. (4 Grand Canal Square, Grand Canal Harbour, D2 Dublin, Ireland). Cookies are used for this purpose, which enable an analysis of the use of the website by its users. The information generated in this way is transferred to the provider&#39;s server and stored there. The data processing is based on the legal provisions of § 96 (3) TKG and Art. 6 (1) lit. a (consent) and/or f (legitimate interest) of the GDPR.</p>
<p>Our concern in terms of the GDPR (legitimate interest) is to improve our offering and our website.</p>
<p>Further details on Facebook&#39;s terms of use and data protection can be found at https://de-de.facebook.com/policies/cookies/.</p>
<h3>Plugins</h3>
<p>To protect input forms on our site, we use the &#34;reCAPTCHA&#34; service provided by Google LLC, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043 USA, hereinafter referred to as &#34;Google&#34;. This service can be used to distinguish whether the input is of human origin or is being misused by automated machine processing.</p>
<p>To the best of our knowledge, the referrer URL, IP address, website visitor behavior, information about the operating system, browser and length of stay, cookies, display instructions and scripts, user input behavior and mouse movements in the &#34;reCAPTCHA&#34; checkbox area are transmitted to &#34;Google&#34;.</p>
<p>Google uses the information obtained in this way to digitize books and other printed materials and to optimize services such as Google Street View and Google Maps (e.g., house number and street name recognition).</p>
<p>The IP address transmitted as part of reCAPTCHA is not merged with other Google data unless you are logged into your Google account when using the reCAPTCHA plug-in. If you want to prevent Google from transmitting and storing data about you and your behavior on our website, you must log out of Google before visiting our site or using the reCAPTCHA plug-in. The use of information obtained through the reCAPTCHA service is governed by the Google Terms of Service.</p>
<p>This website uses the Google Maps product from Google LLC. By using this website, you consent to the collection, processing, and use of automatically collected data by Google LLC, its representatives, and third parties.</p>
<p>The Google Maps Terms of Use can be found at <a href="https://www.google.com/intl/de_de/help/terms_maps/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Google Maps Terms of Use</a>.</p>
<h3>Storage and deletion of data</h3>
<p>In the event of a contract being concluded, all data from the contractual relationship will be stored until the expiry of the applicable tax retention period. The data &#34;name,&#34; &#34;address,&#34; &#34;vouchers ordered,&#34; and &#34;purchase date&#34; will also be stored until the expiry of the statutory or, if applicable, contractually longer periods with regard to warranty and redemption period of vouchers.</p>
<p>After a declared objection, we will ensure that the data is deleted by us and our contract processors, unless there are legal or contractual reasons to the contrary. If the purchase process is canceled, the data transmitted to us up to that point and already stored by us will be deleted in accordance with section 3.2. Data processing is carried out on the basis of the legal provisions of § 96 (3) TKG (Telecommunications Act) and Art. 6 (1) lit. a (consent) and/or lit. b (necessary for contract fulfillment) of the GDPR.</p>
<h3>Your rights</h3>
<p>You have the right to confirmation, information, correction, deletion, restriction, data portability, revocation, and objection. If you believe that the processing of your data violates data protection law or that your data protection rights have been violated in any other way, please contact us directly by email at &#105;&#x6E;&#102;&#x6F;&#64;&#x77;&#97;&#x6E;&#100;&#x65;&#114;&#x68;&#111;&#x74;&#101;&#x6C;&#115;&#x2E;&#99;&#x6F;&#109; or the Austrian Data Protection Authority. General Terms and Conditions for the Purchase of Online Vouchers</p>
<h4>General information</h4>
<p>The contract is concluded with Wanderhotels e.V., Südtiroler Platz 2/3. Stock, 9900 Lienz. Any deviating provisions are only valid if they have been expressly agreed in writing by both parties. Only persons aged 18 and over are entitled to make purchases in our online shop.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<h4>Conclusion of contract, payment, and delivery</h4>
<p>The vouchers offered on the website represent a non-binding and subject-to-change purchase offer. Prices include any applicable sales tax. The online ordering of a voucher via the Internet represents a binding purchase offer by the customer, which Wanderhotels e.V. is entitled to accept within 48 hours by sending an order confirmation via email, thereby concluding the purchase contract. If no order confirmation is received within the aforementioned period, the purchase offer is deemed rejected and no purchase contract is concluded. After receipt of payment of the amount owed under the concluded purchase contract, the purchased vouchers will be sent by Wanderhotels e.V. . To save shipping costs, the purchased vouchers can also be paid for by credit card or instant bank transfer, in which case the vouchers will be sent free of charge via email and can be printed out by the customer. If requested by the customer, the vouchers will also be sent by post even if they are paid for by credit card or instant bank transfer. No liability is accepted for any delay in delivery by post. If the voucher ordered online has already been sent to the customer before the payment for it has been received or credited to Wanderhotels e.V., the voucher is not valid until full payment has been made and Wanderhotels e.V. is entitled to withhold the services specified in the voucher until full payment of the amount due has been received.</p>
</li>
<li>
<h4>Vouchers</h4>
<p>Please note that online vouchers are sent to customers by Wanderhotels e.V. with a forgery-proof code. Since the customer can print the voucher themselves, multiple prints are possible, but only one print is valid and redeemable. The first voucher redeemed in the INCERT voucher management system with the corresponding barcode is considered the original and must be debited immediately after redemption by Wanderhotels e.V. . Should further copies with the same code appear, this constitutes misuse, which will result in criminal prosecution. As a voucher can be passed on or given away, Wanderhotels e.V. is not obliged or able to check the ownership rights of the redeemer. When redeeming, only the following is checked: whether the corresponding barcode has actually been approved by the system and whether the corresponding voucher has actually been paid for. Lost vouchers will not be replaced. Vouchers cannot be returned in exchange for cash. If the value of the voucher exceeds the value of the service consumed, a new voucher will be generated for the remaining value. In such a case, there is no entitlement to a cash payment of the outstanding voucher amount. Wanderhotels e.V. is not obliged to accept unpaid vouchers as a means of payment. Wanderhotels e.V. vouchers can only be redeemed at current member establishments. In hotels that have left the group, the value can neither be credited nor offset. Should Wanderhotels e.V. have to close or cease trading for any reason, the online vouchers shall expire without compensation.</p>
</li>
<li>
<h4>Validity, period of validity</h4>
<p>Vouchers have no expiry date and can be redeemed at any time. Each voucher can only be redeemed once, which is ensured by a barcode or voucher number associated with the voucher.</p>
</li>
<li>
<h4>Cash redemption, invoicing</h4>
<p>Cash redemption of the voucher or the value it represents is not possible. A VAT-compliant invoice with the corresponding tax certificate can only be issued at the time the voucher is redeemed and the service is actually provided.</p>
</li>
<li>
<h4>Security guarantee, data protection</h4>
<p>Your security is our top priority! Therefore, data such as credit card number, bank code, account number, name, and address are transmitted via certified payment providers using their secure SSL connection in accordance with PCI guidelines when paying by credit card. This ensures that no unauthorized person can read the data you enter during transmission over the Internet. To provide additional security in the voucher shop, we apply a series of additional security measures. Your details are processed by us using automated systems. In accordance with the general terms and conditions, the customer agrees to receive advertising information from Wanderhotels e.V. This data will not be passed on to third parties.</p>
